<section class="pub-simple-head"><span class="pub-eyebrow">StockChief</span><h1><%= title %></h1></section>
<section class="pub-legal">
<% if(kind==='/roadmap'){ %>
<p>These are future development areas. They are not promises of current support or delivery dates.</p>
<ul><li>Vendor-qualified ERP integrations, including NetSuite</li><li>Full two-way QuickBooks and Xero accounting sync. Connections for approved journal exports are available today; full two-way accounting sync is planned.</li><li>EDI trading-partner workflows</li><li>SAML single sign-on. Company sign-in using OpenID Connect is available today on Pro and Custom.</li><li>Multi-currency operations</li><li>Multi-company administration and consolidation</li></ul>
<p>Current work focuses on import reliability, inventory accuracy, plan limits, and everyday warehouse operations. <a href="/contact?topic=requirement">Discuss a requirement</a> before relying on a roadmap feature.</p>
<% }else if(kind==='/security'){ %>
<h2>Encryption and credentials</h2><p>Hosted access uses HTTPS. Stored connection credentials use AES-256-GCM encryption. Passwords are stored as salted scrypt hashes; API tokens are stored as hashes. Database encryption and recovery settings depend on the deployed hosting configuration.</p>
<h2>Access control</h2><p>Business records are scoped to an inventory and account. Team permissions, API scopes, plan checks, and approval rules limit operations. Stock movements and posted journal entries retain their history.</p>
<h2>Backups and recovery</h2><p>Database recovery uses the hosting provider's configured backup facilities. Contact support for the retention period and latest restore-test evidence for your deployment; this page does not certify a recovery time.</p>
<h2>Availability and data location</h2><p>See <a href="/status">service status</a> for a current web and database check. A measured uptime SLA is not published here. Deployment region and third-party processing locations must be confirmed for your account before agreeing to a residency requirement.</p>
<h2>SOC 2</h2><p>StockChief does not claim SOC 2 certification or an available SOC 2 report on this page. Independent audit scope and completion dates have not been published. Ask support for current security evidence and contractual requirements.</p>
<p><a href="/privacy">Privacy notice</a> · <a href="/control">Approvals and controls</a> · <a href="/contact?topic=security">Security questions</a></p>
<% }else if(kind==='/status'){ %>
<h2><%= available?'Web and database responding':'Database connection unavailable' %></h2><p>Checked <%= checkedAt %>.</p><p>This checks the current web request and database connection. It does not certify background jobs, payment providers, AI availability, or historical uptime.</p><p><a href="/support?topic=problem">Report a problem</a> · <a href="/security">Security information</a></p>
<% }else{ %>
<p>Public API access requires an eligible plan and a key scoped to your inventory. Create and revoke keys in Settings. Send keys only over HTTPS and keep them out of browser code.</p>
<h2>Authentication</h2><pre>Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY</pre><p>Inventory tokens can have <code>inventory:read</code> and <code>inventory:write</code>. Custom customers can issue an owner token with <code>agent:run</code> for operational reviews.</p>
<h2>Read the activity log</h2><p>On Custom, the inventory owner can issue a key with <code>audit:read</code> for <code>GET /api/v1/public/audit</code>. Filter with <code>from</code>, <code>to</code>, or <code>q</code>. Send the returned <code>nextCursor</code> as <code>after</code> to read the next page.</p>
<h2>Run an Agent review</h2><pre>POST /api/v1/public/agent/jobs
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: YOUR_UNIQUE_OPERATION_KEY

{"review":"stock-health","filter":"YOUR_SKU"}</pre>
<p>Use the returned job ID with <code>GET /api/v1/public/agent/jobs/JOB_ID</code> and the same token to read its status and result. Reviews use the registered jobs in Agent reviews. To run a report you own, send <code>{"review":"saved-report","reportId":"REPORT_ID","page":1}</code>. Use the ID from the saved report’s URL. An optional signed <code>agent.review.completed</code> webhook contains the job ID.</p>
<h2>Start an Agent job</h2><pre>POST /api/v1/public/agent/jobs
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: YOUR_UNIQUE_OPERATION_KEY

{"job":"plan-van-routes"}</pre>
<p>On Custom, the same token starts agent work: <code>plan-van-routes</code>, <code>take-slow-stock-steps</code>, <code>fix-product-data</code>, <code>sort-new-products</code>, <code>retire-discontinued-products</code>, <code>warn-before-expiry</code>, <code>add-landed-costs</code>, <code>book-repeat-pallet-pickups</code>, <code>prepare-export-papers</code>, or <code>run-playbook</code> with <code>"playbook":"PLAYBOOK_ID"</code>. Each job runs through its own settings, job mode and limits. Work that always needs a person, such as paying a supplier, refunds, price changes or write-offs, comes back as <code>waiting_for_person</code> and waits in Needs you. Pause, Watch only and the first 14 days hold the job. Resending the same Idempotency-Key returns the first result. A token can start 30 jobs an hour. Signed <code>agent.job.completed</code>, <code>agent.job.held</code> and <code>agent.job.failed</code> webhooks carry the job ID, its status and what waits.</p>
<h2>Read stock</h2><pre>GET /api/v1/public/inventory?limit=200</pre><p>The response contains <code>data</code> with <code>skuId</code>, <code>code</code>, <code>name</code>, <code>locationId</code>, <code>location</code>, and <code>onHand</code>. Request up to 500 positions per page. Pass the returned <code>nextCursor</code> as <code>cursor</code> until it is null. Preserve the cursor as returned; do not construct it.</p>
<h2>Receive physical stock</h2><pre>POST /api/v1/public/commands/inventory/receive
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: YOUR_UNIQUE_OPERATION_KEY

{"skuId":"YOUR_SKU_ID","locationId":"YOUR_LOCATION_ID","quantity":5,"reference":"Delivery reference"}</pre><p>Lot-tracked stock also needs its lot details; serialized stock needs the exact serials. A physical receipt alone does not establish purchase cost or create a supplier invoice. Use the purchasing workflow when recording a purchase.</p>
<h2>Count physical stock</h2><pre>POST /api/v1/public/commands/inventory/adjust
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: YOUR_UNIQUE_OPERATION_KEY

{"skuId":"YOUR_SKU_ID","locationId":"YOUR_LOCATION_ID","countedQuantity":5,"reasonCode":"physical_count"}</pre><p>The count command is for quantity-tracked products. Reducing fully costed stock also reduces its recorded value. Added units need purchase-cost evidence through the purchasing or opening-stock workflow; a count is not a supplier invoice.</p>
<h2>Signed webhooks</h2><p>Create endpoints in Settings → Connections → Developers. Supported events are <code>stock.changed</code>, <code>purchase_order.received</code> and <code>order.created</code>. The body contains <code>id</code>, <code>type</code>, <code>workspaceId</code>, <code>occurredAt</code> and <code>data</code>. Quantities in stock events are decimal strings.</p><p>Verify <code>X-StockChief-Signature: v1=HEX</code> against HMAC-SHA256 with your signing secret and the exact UTF-8 string <code>X-StockChief-Timestamp + "." + raw_request_body</code>. Compare signatures in constant time, reject timestamps more than five minutes old, and deduplicate by <code>X-StockChief-Event-Id</code>. Parse JSON only after signature verification. Return a 2xx response after durably accepting the event.</p><p>Delivery is at least once, with up to 12 automatic attempts. The event ID and body remain stable across retries; signatures use the current attempt timestamp. Endpoints require public HTTPS, redirects are not followed, and each request has a 10-second timeout. Up to 10 active endpoints are allowed per inventory. Delivery remains subject to API access and API-event allowance; failed attempts do not consume the reserved allowance. Revoking an endpoint stops queued deliveries; a request already in flight may finish.</p>
<h2>Retries and errors</h2><p>Write commands require an idempotency key. Reuse the same key and identical body after an uncertain response. A successful first write returns 201; replay returns 200. Error responses use <code>{"error":{"code":"…","message":"…"}}</code>. Invalid input, expired keys, insufficient scopes, and plan limits must be resolved before retrying.</p>
